  "id": "COMPOUND:22443 - PROTEIN:5826",
  "verbalization": "Ent-Yahazuno is implicated in the biological activity of SMMC-7721 through a series of molecular interactions. The evidence suggests that Ent-Yahazuno acts as a target for multiple compounds, including MIP, 5-Hydroxy-6,8-Dimethoxy-2,3-Dimethylbenzo[G]Chromen-4-One, and Sophoradiol, all of which are targets of SMMC-7721. This indicates that Ent-Yahazuno may be a common point of interaction with these compounds, potentially influencing their activity against SMMC-7721. The shared target relationship implies that Ent-Yahazuno could be a key mediator in the cellular response to these compounds, possibly through a common mechanism or pathway. The evidence supports the notion that Ent-Yahazuno is a relevant target for SMMC-7721, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
